 **What it reconnects:** one thing, the chat's live wire to Servex (`Session.stream`, the server-sent events that bring the AI's replies as they are written). Not Whisper, not the mic, not the agent: those have their own rows on the [Debug tab](/framework/ux/Dictate/doc/debug-tab.md).
 
-**When it shows:** only after the wire has been down for 8 s (`WIRE_GRACE_MS` in `ux/Dictate/chat.js`). Before 2026-10-25 it showed on every drop, and the LAN proxy cuts the wire every 30 s and it is back in a second, so it flashed at random (8 times in 8 s in the probe). Since 2026-11-01 it is no longer a line in the sheet: `dev/Socket/Link.js` owns it, the ONE connection state for both the dev socket and this Servex wire, drawn once as a full-width banner at the very top of the page (the sheet's own row and the dev socket's slim strip are gone): "Servex link down 12 s: Servex answered with an error (restarting?) · Reconnect" (or "Site link down …" when the dev socket is the one that dropped), the seconds counting up. One Reconnect press retries every wire that is down.
+**When it shows:** only after the wire has been down for 8 s (`WIRE_GRACE_MS` in `ux/Dictate/chat.js`). Before 2026-10-25 it showed on every drop, and the LAN proxy cuts the wire every 30 s and it is back in a second, so it flashed at random (8 times in 8 s in the probe). Since 2026-11-01 it is no longer a line in the sheet: `dev/Socket/Link.js` owns it, the ONE connection state for both the dev socket and this Servex wire, drawn once as a full-width banner at the very top of the page (the sheet's own row and the dev socket's slim strip are gone): "Servex link down 12 s: Servex answered with an error (restarting?) · Reconnect" (or "Site link down …" when the dev socket is the one that dropped), the seconds counting up. One Reconnect press retries every wire that is down. Since 2026-11-06 that banner shows only while a voice session depends on Servex (a mic is live or a sentence is still sending); otherwise the same state is a small amber dot on the rail's AI button or in the top corner, hover for the words, press to retry ([dev/Socket/Link.js](../../../dev/Socket/Link.js)).
 
 **A press:** reopens the wire at once and says "trying now…". It never throws, does nothing once the chat is gone or the wire is already open, and ignores a second tap within 0.5 s, so there is never a second wire (`stop.reconnect` in `ext/Session/Session.js`). The "crash" after a press was not the button: the probe pressed it in every state with no page error. It shows exactly when Servex restarts, and a Servex restart also brings the dev server back, which reloads the page (or shows "This page is out of date") right after.
 
